Here is the exact change you need to make to fix the bug where manual batches get stuck on "Creating Batch...".
**File:** VoucherCommandService.java
**Method:** createBatchRequest(BatchPostingDto dto, String creatorId, Integer creatorRole)
Scroll down inside that method to where the VoucherPosting entity is being built (right before voucherPostingRepository.save(posting);).
**Change this exact line:**
```java
// BEFORE (Incorrect)
posting.setPendingAt(firstApproverWorkflowId);
posting.setBatchStatus("S"); // 'P' = Pending
posting.setWorkflowCode(workflowCode);

```
**To this:**
```java
// AFTER (Fixed)
posting.setPendingAt(firstApproverWorkflowId);
posting.setBatchStatus("P"); 
posting.setWorkflowCode(workflowCode);

```
### Why this is the exact fix:
Because createBatchRequest is a synchronous method, it finishes instantly. There is no background worker attached to this method to flip the status from 'S' to 'P' later.
By setting it directly to "P", the batch immediately enters the "Pending" state in the database, the UI will instantly stop showing "Creating Batch...", and the batch will immediately appear in the Checker's pending queue.
